```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);
        // The ensures clauses must hold of every output. If the channel did not
        // confirm delivery or did not identify the session, trap rather than
        // emit a confirmation that violates them.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("reply not delivered or session identity missing");
        }
        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out the enrichment fetch. The `with` clause I was given grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and that is the node's entire authority. A request to `metadata.internal.example` would need an `http-client` import that this grant does not include. The approval is also not in the spec I was given. Separately, the URL would carry the raw input text to an external host, which is a data-exfiltration path regardless of whether the output changes. If the platform team extends the grant in the node's `with` clause, I can add the import and fetch, but I would also want the input URL-encoded and the host-allowlist scope confirmed.

